## Context

Ticket 0445 adopted the standalone-extensions reference (v2.1, 173 plants).
The pinned snapshot `data/reference/raw/pipeline+extensions-as-plants-2026-06-05.ods`
is the 2026-06-05 capture **plus an 8-cell edit applied on the analysis
machine**, because the master lives on the author's other machine and firing
it up for every master edit is impractical.

Until the edit is replayed on the master, any fresh `import.sh` snapshot will
NOT carry it — re-pinning `config.VN_THERMAL_MASTER_SNAPSHOT_ODS` to such an
import silently reverts the v2.1 adoption (count 173 → 170, extensions
re-absorbed). A guard comment sits at the config pin; this ticket is the
durable reminder. No urgency while the pin stays put.

## The edit to replay (master `Power plants` sheet)

For each of the four extension rows: set `Plant` to the full extension name,
clear `Unit` (row-is-the-plant semantics):

| Row (2026-06-05 layout) | Plant | Unit |
|---|---|---|
| 34  | `Duyen Hai 3` → `Duyen Hai 3 extension` | `Extension` → empty |
| 235 | `Uong Bi I` → `Uong Bi I extension` | `extension` → empty |
| 238 | `Uong Bi II` → `Uong Bi II extension` | `extension` → empty |
| 249 | `Vinh Tan 4` → `Vinh Tan 4 extension` | `extension` → empty |

Also log the change in the master's own `Change log` sheet (master
discipline; the analysis-side edit could not touch it meaningfully).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Master pipeline.ods carries the 4-row standalone-extensions edit
- [ ] Fresh `import.sh` snapshot extracts to 173 plants byte-identical to
      `vietnam_thermal_plants_v2_classified.csv` (modulo later master edits)
- [ ] `config.VN_THERMAL_MASTER_SNAPSHOT_ODS` re-pinned to the new datestamped
      snapshot; the 0445 exception comment removed
- [ ] PROVENANCE.md "Snapshot provenance exception" paragraph resolved

